    {
      "ordinal": 3,
      "depth": 0,
      "kind": "section",
      "number": "1",
      "title": "Definition",
      "body": "● Wolf ribs helmets are bascinet-based helmets topped by a central-pivot facial grill. The few available sources are paintings from the Czech Republic and Germany. The primary sources are dated from 1380 and 1450.\n● The helmet is very similar to other bascinets. It is constructed with a center-hinge visor (such as Klappvisor), locked with a “spoon”, and is worn with an aventail.\n● Wolf ribs helmets are approved for 14th-century and transitional armor.\n● Wolf ribs helmets with bascinet shape are denied for 15th century armors.",
      "page_from": 3,
      "page_to": 3,
      "stable_key": "wolfribs:1",
